{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        String s = sc.next();\n        int nk = 0, nv = 0, no = 0;\n        int[] kpos = new int[n], vpos = new int[n], opos = new int[n];\n        int[] snk = new int[n + 1], snv = new int[n + 1], sno = new int[n + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            char ch = s.charAt(i);\n            if (ch == 'V') vpos[nv++] = i;\n            else if (ch == 'K') kpos[nk++] = i;\n            else opos[no++] = i;\n            snk[i + 1] = nk;\n            snv[i + 1] = nv;\n            sno[i + 1] = no;\n        }\n        int INF = (int) 1e9;\n        int[][][][] best = new int[2][nk + 1][nv + 1][no + 1];\n        for (int[][][] x : best) for (int[][] y : x) for (int[] z : y) Arrays.fill(z, INF);\n        best[0][0][0][0] = 0;\n        for (int k = 0; k <= nk; ++k) {\n            for (int v = 0; v <= nv; ++v) {\n                for (int o = 0; o <= no; ++o) {\n                    for (int hv = 0; hv < 2; ++hv) {\n                        int cur = best[hv][k][v][o];\n                        if (k < nk && hv == 0) {\n                            best[0][k + 1][v][o] = Math.min(best[0][k + 1][v][o], cur + Math.max(snv[kpos[k]] - v, 0) + Math.max(sno[kpos[k]] - o, 0));\n                        }\n                        if (v < nv) {\n                            best[1][k][v + 1][o] = Math.min(best[1][k][v + 1][o], cur + Math.max(snk[vpos[v]] - k, 0) + Math.max(sno[vpos[v]] - o, 0));\n                        }\n                        if (o < no) {\n                            best[0][k][v][o + 1] = Math.min(best[0][k][v][o + 1], cur + Math.max(snv[opos[o]] - v, 0) + Math.max(snk[opos[o]] - k, 0));\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        pw.println(Math.min(best[0][nk][nv][no], best[1][nk][nv][no]));\n        pw.close();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    string s;\n    cin >> n >> s;\n\n    int nk = 0, nv = 0, no = 0;\n    vector<int> kpos(n), vpos(n), opos(n);\n    vector<int> snk(n + 1, 0), snv(n + 1, 0), sno(n + 1, 0);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        char ch = s[i];\n        if (ch == 'V') {\n            vpos[nv++] = i;\n        } else if (ch == 'K') {\n            kpos[nk++] = i;\n        } else {\n            opos[no++] = i;\n        }\n        snk[i + 1] = nk;\n        snv[i + 1] = nv;\n        sno[i + 1] = no;\n    }\n\n    const int INF = 1e9;\n    int dim_k = nk + 1;\n    int dim_v = nv + 1;\n    int dim_o = no + 1;\n    int stride_hv = dim_k * dim_v * dim_o;\n    int stride_k = dim_v * dim_o;\n    int stride_v = dim_o;\n    int stride_o = 1;\n\n    vector<int> best(2 * stride_hv, INF);\n    best[0] = 0; // best[0][0][0][0]\n\n    for (int k = 0; k <= nk; ++k) {\n        for (int v = 0; v <= nv; ++v) {\n            for (int o = 0; o <= no; ++o) {\n                for (int hv = 0; hv < 2; ++hv) {\n                    int cur = best[hv * stride_hv + k * stride_k + v * stride_v + o];\n                    if (cur == INF) continue;\n                    if (k < nk && hv == 0) {\n                        int idx = 0 * stride_hv + (k + 1) * stride_k + v * stride_v + o;\n                        best[idx] = min(best[idx], cur + max(snv[kpos[k]] - v, 0) + max(sno[kpos[k]] - o, 0));\n                    }\n                    if (v < nv) {\n                        int idx = 1 * stride_hv + k * stride_k + (v + 1) * stride_v + o;\n                        best[idx] = min(best[idx], cur + max(snk[vpos[v]] - k, 0) + max(sno[vpos[v]] - o, 0));\n                    }\n                    if (o < no) {\n                        int idx = 0 * stride_hv + k * stride_k + v * stride_v + (o + 1);\n                        best[idx] = min(best[idx], cur + max(snv[opos[o]] - v, 0) + max(snk[opos[o]] - k, 0));\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    int ans = min(best[0 * stride_hv + nk * stride_k + nv * stride_v + no],\n                  best[1 * stride_hv + nk * stride_k + nv * stride_v + no]);\n    cout << ans << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.806619057897478e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0003582789213396609, -3.194758028257638e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.9430925021879375e-05, -1.4781842764932662e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.10494892299175262, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.25398215651512146, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, 0.0, -0.5930803418159485, -0.023247193545103073, -0.011053048074245453, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.576194703578949, 0.0, 0.0, -0.12708616256713867, -0.00097441865364